; THE TOP BIT OF THE BYTE AT THIS CELL  taken by halving it seven times and
; keeping the quotient; The byte is REPLACED by its top bit and the pointer
; comes back here; q t and f sit in the three cells above  which is what
; block/halve wants  so this block needs FOUR cells and not one;
;
; IT COSTS ABOUT TWICE THE VALUE and depends on nothing else  which is the
; property that makes it usable inside a constant time argument: the work is
; a function of the byte and not of a secret choice made about it;
;
; THIS TEXT ALREADY EXISTS IN aes/xtime  written out seven times inline  and
; again in idiom/add8's carry; NEITHER IS MIGRATED HERE and that is deliberate
; rather than lazy: a paste reads a callee's committed artifact  and xtime
; is pasted by four files  so the comment change alone would regenerate
; most of the AES tree for no change in instructions; HANDOFF records it;
;
; ASSERT ptr=+0
; halving one of seven; the bit that falls off is not wanted
%%block/halve%%
R2
  [-]
L2
R1
  [-L1+R1]
L1
; halving two of seven; the bit that falls off is not wanted
%%block/halve%%
R2
  [-]
L2
R1
  [-L1+R1]
L1
; halving three of seven; the bit that falls off is not wanted
%%block/halve%%
R2
  [-]
L2
R1
  [-L1+R1]
L1
; halving four of seven; the bit that falls off is not wanted
%%block/halve%%
R2
  [-]
L2
R1
  [-L1+R1]
L1
; halving five of seven; the bit that falls off is not wanted
%%block/halve%%
R2
  [-]
L2
R1
  [-L1+R1]
L1
; halving six of seven; the bit that falls off is not wanted
%%block/halve%%
R2
  [-]
L2
R1
  [-L1+R1]
L1
; halving seven of seven; the bit that falls off is not wanted
%%block/halve%%
R2
  [-]
L2
R1
  [-L1+R1]
L1
; ASSERT ptr=+0
